# This is a static HTML/CSS/JS site -- everything below is the Python ML
# pipeline (offline model training/research), not part of the deployed site.
# Excluding it stops Vercel from mis-detecting this as a Python project.
#
# All paths below are anchored to the repo root with a leading slash. Without
# that, a pattern like "data/" (no leading slash) matches ANY folder named
# "data" at any depth -- including assets/data/, which is where the live
# site's real_prices.json actually lives. That exact bug shipped once already:
# it silently broke every page (blank balances/clock/stock list) because the
# frontend's price fetch 404'd with no visible error.
/notebooks/
/src/
/scripts/
/models/
/data/
/results/
/public/
/docs/
/app/
/.venv/
*.ipynb
/requirements.txt
/kaggle.json
/MarketMinds_Proposal (2).docx.md
/marketminds_design_mockup.html
/image.png
/image11.jpeg
